@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G1 · Writers, checkers and users: the publication workflow
top to bottom direction
$producer(producers, "API authors · Analysis tools · Third-party tools\nWrite an API description (producers)")
$validator(validation, "Validator\nChecks required facts\nand their consistency")
$package(contract, "Published AIL package\nDescribes the chosen API and its contract")
$catalogue(catalogue, "Profile and ABI definitions\nSupply extension rules\nand machine-level rules")
$consumer(consumers, "Binding generators · Documentation renderers\nLLM tools\nUse the same API facts (consumers)")
producers --> validation : submit the description\nunder the same rules
validation --> contract : when checks pass, the producer\ncan publish the complete description
contract -right-> catalogue : selects exact bytes by\nidentifier, version and digest
contract --> consumers : supplies declarations\nand obligations
legend bottom
  Proposed workflow; tools remain future work. Non-normative: L2–L3, C8, A1, A5.
  Checking the description establishes completeness and consistency.
  Library behaviour needs separate evidence from authors, review and implementation testing.
  Rectangle = people or tools writing descriptions; hexagon = validator;
  folder = package; cylinder = definition catalogue; component = tools using descriptions.
  Arrows follow the description. The branch selects shared definitions.
  This overview leaves individual clauses and native calls to the detail pages.
endlegend
@enduml
